{% import "@SyliusShop/Common/Macro/money.html.twig" as money %}

{#
    What the applied gift cards cover and what remains to pay, wherever the shop sums up the cart: below the totals of
    the cart summary, below the summary on the address, shipping and payment steps, and below the order summary on the
    complete step (see SetonoSyliusGiftCardExtension::prepend()). The order is still a cart on all of them. Sylius
    passes it to the cart summary as `cart` and to the checkout's summaries as `order`, so either is taken.

    Sylius fires no template event inside its totals tables, so these figures cannot become rows of them without the
    host application overriding Sylius' templates. They are instead rendered as a segment of their own, built like the
    summaries of the cart and the checkout sidebar, on the events Sylius renders each summary through, with a priority
    that places the segment right below the summary. The gift cards pay for the order rather than discount it, so the
    order total the summaries show stays what the order costs, and this is where the customer sees what is left to pay.

    Amounts go through the `money` macro, like every other figure in the summary, so they follow the display currency
    the shopper picked rather than the currency the order is stored in.
#}
{% set order = cart ?? order %}

{% if order.giftCards is not empty %}
    {% set covered = setono_gift_card_covered_amount(order) %}
    {% if covered > 0 %}
        <div class="ui segment" {{ sylius_test_html_attribute('gift-card-totals') }}>
            <table class="ui very basic table">
                <tbody>
                    <tr {{ sylius_test_html_attribute('gift-cards-total') }}>
                        <td>{{ 'setono_sylius_gift_card.ui.gift_cards'|trans }}:</td>
                        <td class="right aligned">{{ money.convertAndFormat(-covered) }}</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr {{ sylius_test_html_attribute('gift-cards-remaining-total') }}>
                        <td>{{ 'setono_sylius_gift_card.ui.remaining_to_pay'|trans }}:</td>
                        <td class="right aligned">{{ money.convertAndFormat(setono_gift_card_remaining_total(order)) }}</td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    {% endif %}
{% endif %}
